coverage.summary:
Rental properties first built on or before October 1, 1978, plus replacement units under LAMC 151.28. Covered types:
- apartments and duplexes;
- two or more single-family dwellings on one parcel;
- hotel, motel, rooming or boarding house rooms occupied by the same tenant over 30 consecutive days;
- residential units attached to commercial buildings;
- ADUs and JADUs;
- mobile homes and RVs in mobile home parks.

Condominiums and townhomes are covered, but their rent is not regulated for tenancies that commenced after December 31, 1995.

rules.requirement:
Owners who demolish a Protected Unit for new construction within 5 years after filing a Notice of Intent to Withdraw (RSO) or Declaration of Intent to Evict (JCO) must comply with RPO relocation rules. They must pay the highest applicable amount under state law (Housing Crisis Act, Gov. Code § 66300 et seq.) and City law.

All tenants get at least the RSO or JCO amounts within 15 days of the termination notice. Lower-income households (80% AMI or below) get enhanced relocation.

The owner chooses one option:
- Option 1: standardized Chart B payment through the City's relocation consultant.
- Option 2: an LAHD-approved comparable replacement unit plus Chart A amounts.
- Option 3: individualized relocation under an approved plan and private consultant, plus Chart A amounts within 15 days.

Occupant protections:
- right to relocation;
- right to remain up to 6 months before construction starts, including a 6-month notice;
- right to return if demolition does not proceed;
- right of first refusal for some tenants;
- tenant notification.

Penalties start at $250,000 per displaced unit, and LAHD permit clearances can be withheld.
